, by hsienfan. If you're looking for help or inspiration, you could ask him for help, or go to the thread and see what he has done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25563-elcid321","name":"Elcid321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T23:36:31-08:00","id":1525558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead?p=1507542#post1507542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in the Forums after two-year-long depression. Sorry about the necroposting. One day I'll finish this.</div> </div> </div> </div>As ElCid said check out KotE: The Relentless Age.<br /> <br /> I did my own work spinning The Hungry Dead into a worldwide phenomena decades ago but its so much easier with TRAs flexible system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T19:55:49-08:00","id":1525577,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough I've been working on a very similar creature by the same name and likewise inspired by actual folklore for my Werewolf chronicles. I am hitting all the same points made in the original post (probably because we are both using the same myths and folklore as our inspiration.) But I simply made the Strigoi a type of fomori. Technically a human first becomes a fomori while they are alive and have witchlike powers (the Strega), but after they die the fomori transitions to an undead state (the Strigoi) and gain additional powers and the Taint of Special Diet (human flesh and blood). The Bane that transforms them is the Strix or Witch-Owl. They are vampires, but of course, not Kindred. But they could easily pass as such given all the Merits and Flaws out there, and could be easily confused as being from certain clans or Caitiff. Or perhaps thought of as a bloodline.<br /> <br /> I find the fomori concept as an easy way to introduce a lot of monstrous animals or humans that originate in myth, legend, and folklore.<br /> <br /> Since I didn't want them to really duplicate the same game niche the Kindred already occupy, I had to figure out some ways that they were different, and therefore a different kind of opponent for the Garou than the Kindred were. So I made them to work closely together with their local Wyrm witch cult - human recruits, living fomori witches, and undead fomori. They aren't loners and they don't have coteries. They are just part of the same witch cult. I have the Strigoi survive mostly by graverobbing to better hide their own identity and reduce detection by not hunting live humans most of the time. (They have a Special Diet, but they don't have a Hunger like Kindred do.) I make them primarily rural based instead of dwelling in the cities. And they work closely with Banes and are more involved in the Umbra, and the Kindred obviously don't. And from a Garou lore perspective, while the Kindred are servants of the Eater of Souls, the Strigoi are servants of the Beast of War.<br /> <br /> I've just been putting my final details on them, and haven't used them in actual game play yet.<br /> <br /> I liked the idea in Jim Butcher's Dresden Files books that there are three courts of vampires, only one of which translates to what we normally think of as vampires. It caused me to think to the Garou, that &quot;Vampirism&quot; and &quot;Vampires&quot; could simply be a generic category that could place all sorts of Wyrm creatures in. The Kindred (what they call Leeches) is simply the most prominent kind. So I've been slowly adding various more kinds of &quot;vampires&quot; into my Werewolf chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T04:00:45-08:00","id":1525585,"title":"","content":"Welcome back. The idea is good, and I think, since they demand flesh and blood, that their powers are divided between the flesh pool, the physical and material powers, and the blood pool, more spiritual/mental. Like, flesh to heal and blood to hide, or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T08:47:28-08:00","id":1525593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389754-the-hungry-dead?p=1507542#post1507542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in the Forums after two-year-long depression. Sorry about the necroposting. One day I'll finish this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The past few years have been rough for us all!<br /> <br /> For your project I was reading the initial brief and the bit about how to handle &quot;morality&quot; for the Strigoi made me think of the CoD game Deviant: the Renegades. In that game they have two virtues called Conviction and Loyalty. Conviction is their anger at the people who hurt them and gives them drive, Loyalty is their ability to bond with people and care. Instead of a Humanity track, the two Virtues are opposed, basically you can't have more than 5 dots between them, certain actions will raise one, but then end up lowering the other.<br /> <br /> There might be some inspiration you could draw for the Strigoi &quot;walk[ing] a thin path between rational behavior and mindless brutality&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Onyx Path game Scion might also help here, each group has two kind of opposed Virtues with the track represented like this. &quot;Fatalism OO\u00d8OO Audacity&quot; when you take certain actions the filled in dot shifts towards one side or the other. The mechanical effects of Virtues in Scion are kind of a mess, but the basic idea of sliding between two extremes and trying to find balance seems like it would work well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":".  Realized Scion is also a good bit of inspiration and added a paragraph 11-18-2023, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}